Po/SSPG survey", "Expert ratings split between Tossup and Lean R, with one Likely D outlier"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a modest Republican edge in a district that leans right, but a favorable midterm environment, Taylor's fundraising and a recent high-quality poll showing her up four put the race at dead even. Expert ratings cluster at Tossup with some Lean R calls, and markets price the Democrat slightly ahead, so a razor-thin Democratic margin with wide uncertainty fits the evidence.", "watch": "Any late-breaking polling or a shift in the national midterm environment in the final weeks could tip this either way.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Rob Wittman (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Virginia's 1st District pairs a long-serving incumbent, Rob Wittman, against Henrico prosecutor Shannon Taylor, who has made anti-corruption her central message. The district leans Republican by about three points, but the 2026 midterm environment favors Democrats, and Taylor has raised over $2 million and kept pace in a race Wittman himself calls close. Recent polling is thin but slightly favors Taylor, including a September Washington Post survey showing her ahead by four among likely voters.\n\nExpert raters mostly call the race a Tossup, with a few rating it Lean Republican and one outlier calling it a Likely Democratic flip. Prediction markets give the Democrat a modest edge. Wittman holds a large cash advantage and the weight of incumbency, but the fundamentals and polling point to one of the cycle's closest House races.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4506, "margin": -0.72}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4359, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4341, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.4371, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3778, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.3736, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3951, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-09